					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-159979#post-496756</guid>
				<title>Re:</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-159979/scp-615#post-496756</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jun 2009 23:51:37 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Sorts</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>323478</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Well, if the first line says something like "SCP-615 is a large collection of dead and discarded plant matter…" there's no reason to open the next paragraph with "Analysis of SCP-615's composition reveal it to be a mixture of countless pieces of discarded and dead plant material…"</p> <p>The first two paragraphs both basically say that it's a pile of dead plant parts that manages to move around on its own somehow. Maybe change the first paragraph to just say what it is and then use the second paragraph to explain that there's no nervous system or muscle structure and yet this thing moves anyway and then it won't seem so redundant.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
